<title>RUSSIA: Russian T-bill yield falls to 39.96 pct at auction.</title>
<headline>Russian T-bill yield falls to 39.96 pct at auction.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 140-day GKO discount Treasury bills fell to 39.96 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>On November 20, the average annualised yield on an issue of a new tranche of 105-day T-bills was 40.35 percent at an auction.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield at today's auction would be in the range of 38.20 to 41.87 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:  </p>
<p>				     Dec 18	    Nov 20</p>
<p>    Series number		22063	     22044</p>
<p>    Issue volume		 8.00 trln rbls  3.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		1.00 million	  1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	    10.71 trln	 4.88 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	     6.96 trln	 2.98 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		     6.04 trln	 2.67 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	     86.71 pct	 89.60 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price   86.55 pct	 89.52 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	     39.96 pct	 40.35 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield  40.52 pct	 40.70 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			 140 days	   105 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date	     May 7, 1997	March 5, 1997</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry also repaid on Wednesday about 6.12 trillion roubles in maturing three-month T-bills (series 21069).</p>
<p>--Nigel Stephenson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
